what do Americans do all day  the government's released its annual  look at how Americans spend their time  it's an interesting snapshot into the  daily lives of the average Joe or Jane  let's start with work Americans do  nearly eight hours of it on a weekday  versus five and a half hours on a  Saturday or Sunday across the entire  week that means nearly seven and a half  hours of work each day but 95% of  Americans have some time each day for  fun or what the Bureau of Labor  Statistics terms the leisure activities  in 2013 an ordinary adult without kids  at home spent four and a half hours on  these leisure activities if you add kids  into the mix that dropped to three and a  half but a hundred and sixty eight  minutes a day TV was the biggest time  suck in the land of the couch potato in  fact Americans only left their couches  to socialize with other Americans 43  minutes each day and if you're not at  work or watching TV or occasionally  doing some exercise you're either asleep  or apparently doing household chores on  a day that included chores the average  woman spent half an hour more on them  than the average man don't worry though  once you're retired it does apparently  get easier in fact if you're 75 or older  you spend around half your waking day in  2013 that's seven and a half hours  having some kind of fun reading  accounted for two hours of every weekend  for that same older demographic while 15  to 19 year-olds spent around the same  period of time  on a computer or playing games on an  average weekend those same American  teenagers spent just four minutes  reading a book the survey doesn't  mention iPads off campus
 

